From 8e7aac65a1b3ea4650f471a52a6d7510fe31de6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvn13 <from.github@bvn13.me>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:27:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(sidebar): let the sidebar be resized

The desktop sidebar has been fixed at 288px (md:w-72). On wide screens that
wastes space; with long project names it truncates everything.

A drag handle on its right edge sets the width, clamped to 220-640px and
persisted in localStorage. Double-click or Home resets it, the arrow keys
adjust it in 16px steps, and the mobile drawer is untouched.

The width lives in its own hook rather than in useUiPreferences, which stores
booleans only (parseBoolean, VALID_KEYS).
