From df342846aeffbfbce3bebbf18a319b0ddb9ab550 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvn13 <from.github@bvn13.me>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 10:51:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(sidebar): end an in-flight resize when the layout
 goes mobile

The separator only ends a drag through its own pointerup/pointercancel.
When isMobile flips mid-drag the desktop branch unmounts it while
AppContentInner stays mounted, so that never fires: the body keeps
userSelect: none, a queued frame stays queued, and the live resize origin
makes a plain hover over the remounted handle resize the sidebar once the
desktop layout returns. An [isMobile] effect ends the drag instead; the
unmount cleanup stays for the case it already covered.

parseSidebarWidth used parseInt, which takes a numeric prefix, so a stored
'320px' resolved to 320 rather than the default its docstring promises.

Raised by CodeRabbit on PR #1189.
