From 2fdbba392f61e67bb5a58a424f171805b5c21069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvn13 <from.github@bvn13.me>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:30:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(sidebar): collapse the section tabs that no longer
 fit into a dropdown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The section strip was written for a fixed 288px sidebar: four tabs in a flex
row, two of them growing. Once the sidebar became resizable, dragging it
towards its 220px minimum pushed Conversations and the two icon tabs out over
the panel edge instead of shrinking the row.

The strip now measures itself and keeps only the tabs it has room for; the rest
move into a "…" dropdown at its right edge. The widths come from an off-layout
copy of the full strip, because a tab that has already been dropped is no
longer in the row to measure, and a ResizeObserver re-runs the split while the
sidebar is dragged.

The tab of the section on screen is always kept in the row, even when it is the
one that would have fallen past the fold, so the strip still shows where you
are.

The desktop and mobile headers carried two near-identical copies of the markup
and now share SidebarModeTabs. The only behaviour that differed was a mobile-only
screen-reader label on Running; both headers now label every icon-only tab.

