From 7255ecde9adda95dfdd481539aba7e09e5c6c41f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvn13 <from.github@bvn13.me>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:47:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(sidebar): drop the resize handle when the sidebar is
 hidden
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hide sidebar swaps the panel for a 48px icon rail, but the region kept the
stored width pinned on its container, so the rail sat in a 288px box with the
border and the drag handle still drawn at the far edge — a vertical line down
the screen next to a sidebar that was supposed to be gone.

The width and the handle now apply only while the full sidebar is on screen.
The collapsed rail sizes itself again, as it did before the sidebar became
resizable.

The guard that ends an in-flight drag now keys on whether resizing is available
at all, so collapsing mid-drag releases the body's userSelect the same way going
mobile already did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
